    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] design MOFs with amine-functionalized micropores using 3-amino-1,2,4-triazole as the ligand → enables a framework concept aimed at selective low-partial-pressure CO2 capture"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] use oxalate as a co-ligand to bridge Zn-Atz layers → favors formation of the porous target framework instead of entirely different dense frameworks"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "compound 1 vs the compared Zn-triazolate framework with spaces occupied by oxalate ligand: winner=subject_a on porosity"
